  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Northern White-cheeked Crested Gibbon in Pu Mat National Park, Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will accomplish the following objectives to help secure the biodiversity values of Pu Mat National park focusing on the critically endangered northern white-cheeked gibbon (Nomascus leucogenys) and establish &quot;no kill&quot; zones int the Pu Mat National Park by: (1) Identifying key locations for nothern white-cheeked gibbons and Saola for protection within Pu Mat National Park by performing a desktop study and engaging Saola Technical Working Group. (2) Engaging local communities in forest protection by setting up community-based patrolling and training in surrounding villages. (3) Supporting imporovement of enforcement model of Pu Mat National Park by training rangers in SMART.</narrative>
  </description>
